      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3303d01d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: toxicity; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a humorous and exaggerated comparison between Chevrolet and Ford owners' attitudes toward off-roading, using visual contrast to imply that Chevy owners are more 'muddy' and Ford owners are more 'dramatic' or 'showy'. While not overtly abusive or hateful, it relies on brand-based stereotypes that can be seen as dismissive or mocking of Ford enthusiasts. The intent is to create a lighthearted, relatable joke among car enthusiasts, but the underlying tone may unintentionally alienate or stereotype a group based on brand loyalty, which falls under the category of 'harmful' or 'propaganda' if interpreted as promoting division among car communities. The meme does not contain explicit hate speech or targeted abuse, but the brand-based caricature can be seen as a form of 'harmful' content due to its potential to reinforce negative stereotypes or create unnecessary friction among enthusiasts.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_2254810d"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
